.TH CHAIN-OPERATOR 1 "November 19, 2026" "Cura CLI 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chain-operator \- query Cura Chain balances and transfer assets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chain-operator
.RB [ \-\-help | \-\-version | \-\-manual ]
.br
.B chain-operator balance
.I ADDRESS
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B chain-operator transfer
.RI "key-options amount-options"
.BI \-\-to " ADDRESS"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B chain-operator address
.I key-options
.br
.B chain-operator receipt
.I TXHASH
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A standalone chain client. Desk login is not required.
Asset addresses, names and precision are shared with mm-desk through
assets.json.
Transfer encoding follows the supplied transfer.py reference. Private-key
signing uses native libsecp256k1 through coincurve.
.PP
Use --help or COMMAND --help for command options. --manual opens this page
with the system man(1) viewer and its normal pager configuration.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS balance
.B balance ADDRESS [--limit N] [--rpc-url URL] [--timeout SECONDS] [--json]
.PP
Query any Cura account address. balances and check-balance are aliases.
Follows leaf_getLeafByOwner cursors. The page limit is between 1 and 1000;
the default is 1000. A repeated page is an error, not a duplicated balance.
.PP
Amounts are aggregated exactly. Unknown asset precision is not inferred.
This query reports account balance leaves; transfer selection separately
requires unspent, unlocked, non-pending leaves.
.SS transfer
.B transfer --to ADDRESS (--key-file FILE | --master-file FILE) --token TOKEN
.br
.B (--amount DECIMAL | --raw-amount INTEGER) [options]
.PP
Build a signed transfer with receiver output and change, then simulate it.
The default is dry-run: no transaction is broadcast without --yes.
.TP
.BI \-\-to " ADDRESS"
Destination Cura account address, not its EVM address.
.TP
.BI \-\-key-file " FILE"
32-byte secp256k1 private key as hexadecimal text. No private-key argument
value is accepted directly on the command line.
.TP
.BI \-\-master-file " FILE"
Derive the chain key from an mm-keys.py master seed. Mutually exclusive
with --key-file.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
Configured asset name or operator address.
.TP
.BI \-\-amount " DECIMAL"
Amount in token units. Converted exactly using assets.json precision.
No exponent or fractional smallest unit is accepted.
.TP
.BI \-\-raw-amount " INTEGER"
Positive amount in smallest units. Mutually exclusive with --amount.
.TP
.BI \-\-leaf " ADDRESS"
Select an input leaf. Repeat to select several. Duplicates and mixed asset
IDs are rejected. By default, select largest eligible leaves first.
.TP
.BI \-\-chain-id " INTEGER"
EIP-712 chain ID. Default: 111111111111 (testnet).
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Simulate only; this is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Submit after a successful simulation. Never automatically resubmits.
Mutually exclusive with --dry-run.
.TP
.B \-\-no-wait
Return after the node accepts submission, without waiting for finality.
.TP
.BI \-\-wait-timeout " SECONDS"
Finality deadline. Default: 120 seconds.
.SS address
.B address (--key-file FILE | --master-file FILE) [--json]
.PP
Print the public Cura account address and EVM address. Does not access the
network or print the private key.
.SS receipt
.B receipt TXHASH [--owner ADDRESS] [--wait] [--wait-timeout SECONDS]
.PP
Query a transaction receipt. --wait polls until Finalized, Failed,
Conflicted, or the deadline. --owner supplies the x-app-key routing header.
This command never submits a transaction.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
Network commands accept the following options after the command name.
.TP
.BI \-\-rpc-url " URL"
Chain JSON-RPC endpoint. Default: https://rpc.testnet.curated.finance.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
HTTP request timeout. Default: 15 seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Use JSON output. Balance queries otherwise show a table. Transfer,
address and receipt results are JSON in either mode. Progress goes to stderr.
.SH TRANSFER RESULTS
A successful dry-run reports status dry_run and submitted false.
With --yes, submitted means the node accepted the transaction; finalized
means a finalized receipt was observed. The locally computed transaction
hash must match the node's response.
.PP
A submission timeout or connection loss can leave execution uncertain.
The error retains the transaction hash. Query its receipt before deciding
to resubmit. A finality timeout does not roll back a submitted transfer.
.SH DESK TRANSFERS
Use mm-desk's transfer to-desk command for deposit_pool, and transfer
from-desk for mm_withdraw. Sending an ordinary chain transfer to the pool
owner is not the desk deposit protocol.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CHAIN_OPERATOR_PYTHON
Python executable override. The launcher otherwise uses the adjacent
\&.venv/bin/python when present, then python3.
.TP
.BR MANPAGER , " PAGER"
Interpreted by the system man viewer according to its normal rules.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B markets.json
Testnet trading pair parameters, keyed by desk book. Includes source and date.
.TP
.B assets.json
Shared address-to-asset-name and decimal precision registry. Restart
commands after editing. Display annotations never alter request addresses.
.TP
.B requirements.txt
Pinned dependencies for the shared Python environment.
.TP
.B EXAMPLES.md
Separate command examples for both tools.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful query, simulation, requested submission, or help display.
.TP
.B 1
Validation, simulation, RPC, submission or finality failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line syntax.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted. A submitted transaction may still execute.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mm-desk (1),
.BR man (1),
.BR less (1)
